  ('c83e993e-e27b-5aa9-a2c7-e4c15e6ec088', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'The usual time-management techniques don''t work because____. [A] what they can offer does not ease the modern mind他们所能提供的一切，都无法安抚现代人焦灼的内心。 [B] what challenging books demand is repetitive reading有深度、有难度的书籍，需要人们反复阅读。 [C] what people often forget is carrying a book with them人们常常忘了随身带上一本书。 [D] what deep reading requires cannot be guaranteed深度阅读所必需的条件，无法得到保障。 考研中的but：两个 but 都没有反转、对立、全部是顺着原有观点往 下推进、加重重点。 20 段首 What makes the problem thornier is that the usual time-management techniques don''t seem sufficient.......常规时间管理方法似乎不够用。 转折 But in my experience, using such methods to free up the odd 30 minutes doesn''t work........ 想靠这类时间管理法挤出零散的半小时，根本行不通 段尾 Deep reading requires not just time, but a special kind of time not obtained merely by becoming more efficient. 深度阅读需要的不只是普通时间，而是一种特殊时段 —— 仅靠提升效率根本挤不出来。 原题： 21 What makes the problem thornier is that the usual time-management techniques don''t seem sufficient. The web''s full of articles offering tips on making time to read: "Give up TV" or "Carry a book with you at all times." But in my experience, using such methods to free up the odd 30 minutes doesn''t work. Sit down to read and the flywheel of work-related thoughts keeps spinning—or else you''re so exhausted that a challenging book''s the last thing you need.The modern mind, Tim Parks, a novelist and critic, writes, "is overwhelmingly inclined toward communication... It is not simply that one is interrupted; it is that one is actually inclined to interruption." Deep reading requires not just time, but a special kind of time which can''t be obtained merely by becoming more efficient. 在英语阅读中，快速把握段落大意的确可以通过关注段首、段尾和转折处来实现。这是英语文章常见的 结构特点，尤其是学术类或议论文体', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句3-主表同从.pdf', 19, true, 167, null),
  ('61a51739-da62-5af8-8dba-92182b1aa108', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', '段首句（Topic Sentence）多数段落的主旨句出现在段首，作者直接表明核心观点。', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句3-主表同从.pdf', 21, true, 168, null),
  ('b1bfffa7-0d5e-5585-8362-ceda47c874fe', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', '段尾句（Conclusion Sentence）部分段落会在结尾总结观点，尤其是段内存在层层论证时。', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句3-主表同从.pdf', 21, true, 169, null),
  ('8b847316-3fc7-594e-85d1-f34a1281e785', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', '转折处，转折词（如 but, however, yet,）后的内容往往是作者的真实意图。 分析干扰选项：如何分清表层现象和根本原因 22 But in my experience, using such methods to free up the odd 30 minutes doesn''t work. Sit down to read and the flywheel of work-related thoughts keeps spinning—or else you''re so exhausted that a challenging book''s the last thing you need.The modern mind, Tim Parks, a novelist and critic, writes, "is overwhelmingly inclined toward communication... It is not simply that one is interrupted; it is that one is actually inclined to interruption."', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句3-主表同从.pdf', 21, true, 170, null),
  ('11091d44-4389-5203-b3c6-70ccaa303e6a', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'The usual time-management techniques don''t work because____. [A] what they can offer does not ease the modern mind他们所能提供的一切，都无法安抚现代人焦灼的内 心。【细节信息：属于表层现象】 如何判断是底层原因还是表层症状 细节论据：出现动作场景：sit down Sit down to read ,thoughts keeps spinning 等具体行为 个人感受、情绪描写：exhausted，a challenging book 主观体验 分析干扰选项：如何分清表层现象和根本原因 23 But in my experience, using such methods to free up the odd 30 minutes doesn''t work. Sit down to read and the flywheel of work-related thoughts keeps spinning—or else you''re so exhausted that a challenging book''s the last thing you need.The modern mind, Tim Parks, a novelist and critic, writes, "is overwhelmingly inclined toward communication... It is not simply that one is interrupted; it is that one is actually inclined to interruption."Deep reading requires not just time, but a special kind of time which can''t be obtained merely by becoming more efficient.', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句3-主表同从.pdf', 22, true, 171, null),
  ('faec3d61-9cf1-501d-884a-919257664d24', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'The usual time-management techniques don''t work because____. [D] what deep reading requires cannot be guaranteed深度阅读所必需的条件，无法得到保障。 底层原因：拔高概括，跳出具体小事，讲事物内在本质、核心条件、根本矛盾 分析干扰选项：BC为什么错？？ 24 But in my experience, using such methods to free up the odd 30 minutes doesn''t work. Sit down to read and the flywheel of work-related thoughts keeps spinning—or else you''re so exhausted that a challenging book''s the last thing you need.The modern mind, Tim Parks, a novelist and critic, writes, "is overwhelmingly inclined toward communication... It is not simply that one is interrupted; it is that one is actually inclined to interruption."Deep reading requires not just time, but a special kind of time which can''t be obtained merely by becoming more efficient.', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句3-主表同从.pdf', 23, true, 172, null),
  ('b86b3bfc-a212-5382-a1c2-44de298cb5e1', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'The usual time-management techniques don''t work because____. [A] what they can offer does not ease the modern mind他们所能提供的一切，都无法安抚现代人焦灼的内 心。【细节信息：属于表层现象】 [B] what challenging books demand is repetitive reading有深度、有难度的书籍，需要人们反复阅读。 [C] what people often forget is carrying a book with them人们常常忘了随身带上一本书。 [D] what deep reading requires cannot be guaranteed深度阅读所必需的条件，无法得到保障。 分析干扰选项BC 25 What makes the problem thornier is that the usual time-management techniques don''t seem sufficient. The web''s full of articles offering tips on making time to read: "Give up TV" or "Carry a book with you at all times." But in my experience, using such methods to free up the odd 30 minutes doesn''t work. Sit down to read and the flywheel of work-related thoughts keeps spinning—or else you''re so exhausted that a challenging book''s the last thing you need.', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句3-主表同从.pdf', 24, true, 173, null),
  ('d098e95f-2626-57f2-95f9-6dda04f5b164', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'The usual time-management techniques don''t work because____. [B] what challenging books demand is repetitive reading有难度的书籍所需要的，是反复研读。 【细节拼凑，无中生有，观点符合大家认知，容易让大家产生主观臆断】 [C] what people often forget is carrying a book with them人们常常忽略的一件事，是随身带着一本书。 【通过细节拼凑+自己增加what people often forget而无中生有】 总结：如何避坑，重点句+重点复现词 26 That everyone’s too busy these days is a cliché. But one specific complaint is made especially mournfully: There’s never any time to read. What makes the problem thornier is that the usual time-management techniques don''t seem sufficient. The web''s full of articles offering tips on making time to read: "Give up TV" or "Carry a book with you at all times." But in my experience, using such methods to free up the odd 30 minutes doesn''t work. Sit down to read and the flywheel of work-related thoughts keeps spinning—or else you''re so exhausted that a challenging book''s the last thing you need.The modern mind, Tim Parks, a novelist and critic, writes, "is overwhelmingly inclined toward communication... It is not simply that one is interrupted; it is that one is actually inclined to interruption." Deep reading requires not just time, but a special kind of time which can''t be obtained merely by becoming more efficient.', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句3-主表同从.pdf', 25, true, 174, null),
  ('c3dd3ac4-a297-52eb-8a08-cf5100bbeba0', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'The usual time-management techniques don''t work because____. [A] what they can offer does not ease the modern mind[B] what challenging books demand is repetitive reading [C] what people often forget is carrying a book with them [D] what deep reading requires cannot be guaranteed 真题演练三 略读方法一：复现词 27 The great question is who should benefit from the analysis of all the data generated by our lives now . Privacy law builds on the concept of damage to an individual from identifiable knowledge about them. The data of an individual there gains its value only when it is compared with the data of countless millions more. The use of privacy law to curb the tech giants in this instance feels slightly maladapted. This practice does not address the real worry. It is not enough to say that the algorithms developed by DeepMind will benefit patients and save lives. What matters is that they will belong to a private monopoly, with public resources used to develop them.', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句3-主表同从.pdf', 26, true, 175, null),
