  ('49d7f18a-f1cc-5d43-8535-223dc01256be', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'A stand忍受 B cope C approve批准/同意 D retain保留 31 原文分析：上下文：前文：无家可归者占美国人口的比例越来越大， homelessness（无家可归问题）已达 到如此严重的程度（such proportions）。 后文：地方政府无法可能______。联邦政府必须支持职业培训计划来帮助无家可归者……帮助日益增长的 无家可归者变得越来越困难。 逻辑关系：前文强调问题严重（such proportions），后文提到地方政府无法“应对”或“处理”这一问题，因此 需要联邦政府介入。空格处需填入一个表示“应对”或“处理”的动词，体现地方政府能力不足。 选项匹配[A] stand（忍受/站立）：“can''t possibly stand”意为“无法忍受”，但“忍受”与“问题严重性”搭配不够 准确，更侧重主观感受。[B] cope（应对/处理）：“can''t possibly cope”意为“无法应对”，直接对应地方政府 无力解决无家可归问题，符合语境。[C] approve（批准/同意）：与上下文无关，无家可归问题不需要“批 准”。[D] retain（保留/保持）：与上下文无关，语义不匹配。排除法[A] 虽勉强可通，但不如[B]精准；[C]和 [D]完全无关。[B]是唯一能准确表达“地方政府无力应对”的选项。 目的状语从句—非重点部分 逻辑连词 33 逻辑连词 中文 区别 so that...... 以便 如何区别so that是表示结 果，还是表示目的？', null, '[B] cope', '', '英语2/长难句6-状语从句【预习版】.pdf', 30, true, 201, null),
  ('2ff32b9c-b984-5285-ac2f-3a129e9edd7a', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', '上下文：已经发生了， 是结果；还没发生目的', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句6-状语从句【预习版】.pdf', 33, true, 202, null),
  ('7aec10ff-b633-558e-81ff-0adc3f915a5a', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', '有没有+情态动词，情态 动词表示推测，一般都是 没发生的事，所以是目的 in order that....... 表示目的 考点一：多个状从阅读法 34 when you meet a person for the first time，make an effort to find the things which you and that person have in common so that you can build the conversation from that point. 当你初次与某人见面时，要努力找出你和对方之间的共同之处，这样你就能从这些共同点出发来对话。', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句6-状语从句【预习版】.pdf', 33, true, 203, null),
  ('b41c1f8e-bc2e-5397-b973-c763654ad4ac', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', '找所有动词 meet，make，to find，have，can build', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句6-状语从句【预习版】.pdf', 34, true, 204, null),
  ('13956ec8-128f-523c-b069-bd3d2151c0ac', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', '非谓语动词词组 to find the things', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句6-状语从句【预习版】.pdf', 34, true, 205, null),
  ('d3489d60-f08f-5034-80d2-1c97ad28ef41', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', '从句', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句6-状语从句【预习版】.pdf', 34, true, 206, null),
  ('86c37b52-9a30-52c9-a989-e91caeb710b3', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'which you and that person have in common', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句6-状语从句【预习版】.pdf', 34, true, 207, null),
  ('ad29aa65-ed51-5c16-94a4-f50c4809ba47', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'so that you can build the conversation from that point that point 指的是什么？', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句6-状语从句【预习版】.pdf', 34, true, 208, null),
  ('fdf9448b-59d2-5dd6-b6d4-84a4eeaeb46e', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'when you meet a person for the first time 4 主句 make an effort 真题演练一 35', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句6-状语从句【预习版】.pdf', 34, true, 209, null),
  ('258ec819-d16c-56fb-a081-0d10b9c5615f', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'In the European corporate workplace, generally______. [A] women take the lead [B] men have the final say [C] corporate governance is overwhelmed [D] senior management is family-friendly overwhelm这个词重点掌握，真题高频词 41 Overwhelming majorities of both groups said（that） they believe（that） it is harder for young people today to get started in life than it was for earlier generations. 绝大多数两组人都认为，如今年轻人开始独立生活比前几代人更难 42', null, '[B] men have the final say', '原文核心信息：欧洲企业高层性别不平等（"not a gender-equality heaven"）。
关键数据：女性仅占董事会席位的 14%，高层职位 "overwhelmingly male"（绝大多数为男性）。
职场环境 "never be completely family-friendly"（对家庭不友好）除非女性参与高层决策。
选项分析：[A] women take the lead（女性主导）→ 与原文矛盾，原文强调男性占主导地位。
[B] men have the final say（男性掌握最终决定权）→ 符合原文“高层绝大多数为男性”的描述，且女性
参与决策不足。
[C] corporate governance is overwhelmed（公司治理不堪重负）→ 原文未提及“不堪重负”，属于无关
选项。
[D] senior management is family-friendly（高层管理对家庭友好）→ 原文明确说职场 "never
completely family-friendly"，直接排除。排除法：[A]、[C]、[D] 均与原文冲突或无支持，仅 [B] 与数据
和高层性别比例一致。
地点状语从句—非重点部分
逻辑连词
44
And one of the easiest ways to segment（v 划分） a market is to magnify（v 扩大） gender（n 性别）
differences——or invent(v 发明） them where they did not previously（adv 以前地） exist（v. 存在）.
市场细分最简单的策略之一，就是刻意放大性别差异——甚或在原本并无差异的地方（刻意）制造差异。', '英语2/长难句6-状语从句【预习版】.pdf', 40, true, 211, null),
  ('eb235ac9-6950-5a94-8ae8-a954515f79d0', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', '找所有动词 to segment；is； to magnify；invent；did not exist', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句6-状语从句【预习版】.pdf', 44, true, 212, null),
  ('1d85892e-f4ba-527d-8674-3e6c4ecb2f41', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', '去掉非谓语动词以及其词组', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句6-状语从句【预习版】.pdf', 44, true, 213, null),
  ('86bbfe5c-642d-5459-8f9f-30bf11a33c19', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'to segment a market', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句6-状语从句【预习版】.pdf', 44, true, 214, null),
  ('1a0d6e56-a82a-599c-a000-892de47adff5', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'to magnify gender differences or（to） invent them', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句6-状语从句【预习版】.pdf', 44, true, 215, null),
  ('711ad991-f7a1-5225-85af-0cea6ee37b27', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', '从句', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句6-状语从句【预习版】.pdf', 44, true, 216, null),
  ('5d3b2b63-5e84-57fe-83b4-16550e4822a7', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'where they did not previously exist 4 主句 one of the easiest ways is to A and to B 真题演练一 45 ①Girls’attraction to pink may seem unavoidable, somehow encoded in their DNA, but it is not. ②I had not realised how profoundly marketing trends dictated our perception of what is natural to kids, including our core beliefs about their psychological development. Take the toddler. It was popularized as a marketing trick by clothing manufactures in the 1930s. ③Trade publications counselled department stores that, in order to increase sales, they should create a "third stepping stone" between infant wear and older kids'' clothes. It was only after "toddler" became a common shoppers'' term that it evolved into a broadly accepted developmental stage. Splitting kids, or adults, into ever-timer categories has proved a sure-fire way to boost profits. And one of the easiest ways to segment a market is to magnify gender differences or invent them where they did not previously exist. It can be concluded that girls'' attraction to pink seems to be_____ . 真题演练一 46 It can be concluded that girls'' attraction to pink seems to be_____ . [A] fully understood by clothing manufacturers服装生产商完全理解 [B] clearly explained by their inborn tendency可以由她们与生俱来的倾向清晰解释 [C] mainly imposed by profit-driven businessmen主要是受利益驱动的商人强加造成的 [D] well interpreted by psychological experts被心理学专家充分解读 干扰项分析 47 ①Girls’attraction to pink may seem unavoidable, somehow encoded in their DNA, but it is not. ②Take the toddler. It was popularized as a marketing trick by clothing manufactures in the 1930s. ③Trade publications counselled department stores that, in order to increase sales, they should create a "third stepping stone" between infant wear and older kids'' clothes. ④And one of the easiest ways to segment a market is to magnify gender differences or invent them where they did not previously exist. 女孩子被红色的衣服吸引，是因为市场营销策略导致的，衣服厂商为了赚钱，他们创造了性别差异 It can be concluded that girls'' attraction to pink seems to be_____ . [A] fully understood by clothing manufacturers服装生产商完全理解 [B] clearly explained by their inborn tendency可以由她们与生俱来的倾向清晰解释 [C] mainly imposed by profit-driven businessmen主要是受利益驱动的商人强加造成的 [D] well interpreted by psychological experts被心理学专家充分解读 48 文章主旨：文章指出女孩对粉色的喜爱并非天生，而是由市场营销策略塑造的。商家通过细分市场（如创造 “toddler”这一概念）和放大性别差异来提升利润，粉色与女孩的关联正是这种商业策略的结果。 选项分析：[A] 服装制造商完全理解：文章提到制造商利用营销策略，但未提及他们“完全理解”女孩对粉色的 喜爱，而是强调他们人为制造了这种趋势。[B] 由先天倾向明确解释：文章明确否定这一点（首句指出“not encoded in their DNA”）。[C] 主要由利润驱动的商人强加：与文章内容一致。商家通过细分市场和放大性别 差异（如推广粉色）来提升利润，说明这种吸引力是商业利益驱动的结果。[D] 心理学专家合理解释：文章 未提及心理学专家的角色，重点在商业策略。 比较状语从句—非重点部分 比较逻辑连词 50 逻辑连词 中文 备注 than 比....多/少 than前边是比较级，后边+ 句子，才是比较状语从句 as 和...相比.... Overwhelming majorities of both groups said（that） they believe（that） it is harder for young people today to get started in life than it was for earlier generations. The climate change（that） we are hastening could one day leave us with forests that emit more carbon than they absorb. 真题演练一： 51 ①Even in traditional offices, "the lingua franca of corporate America has gotten much more emotional and much more right-brained than it was 20 years ago," said Harvard Business School professor Nancy Koehn. ②She started spinning off examples. ③"If you and I parachuted back to Fortune 500 companies in 1990, we would see much less frequent use of terms like journey, mission, passion. ④There were goals, there were strategies, there were objectives, but we didn''t talk about energy; we didn''t talk about passion."', null, '[C]。文章明确说明女孩对粉色的偏好是商家为利润人为强加的（如第三段末句）。', '', '英语2/长难句6-状语从句【预习版】.pdf', 44, true, 217, null),
  ('790ce04c-7d30-53ef-9c03-d702296f8ecf', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'According to Nancy Koehn, office language has become ______. [A] less strategic [B] less energetic [C] more objective [D] more emotional 52 原文分析 关键引述：Nancy Koehn指出："美国企业通用语言比20年前更加情感化和右脑化（much more emotional and much more right-brained）"。 对比1990年：当时更多使用"goals, strategies, objectives"等理性词汇，较少使用"journey, mission, passion"等感性词汇。 核心变化：过去：强调战略目标（strategic, objective）现在：强调情感表达（emotional, passionate） 选项匹配[A] less strategic：原文未说战略减少，而是表达方式转变。[B] less energetic：与原文 "energy/passion"增多的描述矛盾。[C] more objective：与"emotional"趋势相反。[D] more emotional： 直接对应"much more emotional"。 方式状语从句—非重点部分 逻辑连词 54 逻辑连词 中文 as 按照....方式 as if 好像，仿佛：用于表示某事物或行为看 起来像是另一种情况，但实际上并非如 此 真题演练一 55 Carry a book with you at all times can actually work, too — providing you dip in often enough, so that reading becomes the default state from which you temporarily surface to take care of business, before dropping back down.On a really good day，it no longer feels as if you are “making time” to read，” but just reading and making time for everything', null, '[D] more emotional', '', '英语2/长难句6-状语从句【预习版】.pdf', 51, true, 218, null),
  ('87afdc7d-2044-525f-978f-e8658ed2b047', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', '"''Carry a book with you at all times'' can work if ______." [A] reading becomes your primary business of the day [B] all the daily business has been promptly dealt with [C] you are able to drop back to business after reading [D] time can be evenly split for reading and business Recap 56 Thanks.', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句6-状语从句【预习版】.pdf', 55, true, 219, null),
